## 🔐 Permissions (Who can do what?)
```bash
chmod 644 file        # rw-r--r--
chmod 755 file        # rwxr-xr-x
chmod +x script.sh    # make executable

chown user:group file # change owner
chgrp group file      # change group

umask 022             # default permission rules

getfacl file          # view advanced permissions
setfacl -m u:user:rwx file  # give custom access
```

### 🧠 chmod in simple terms
```
7 = read + write + execute
6 = read + write
5 = read + execute
4 = read only
```

Example:
```bash
chmod 700 file.txt
```

💡 *Think: Owner | Group | Others → (7 5 5)*

