## ⚙️ Processes & Jobs (What's running?)
```bash
ps aux              # list everything
top                 # live process monitor
htop                # better UI (if installed)

pgrep name          # find process ID
pkill name          # kill by name

kill PID            # kill using ID
killall name        # kill all matching

nice -n 10 cmd      # start with priority
renice -n 10 -p PID # change priority

jobs                # background jobs
bg %1               # run in background
fg %1               # bring to front

nohup cmd &         # run even after logout

time cmd            # measure execution time
watch -n 1 free     # repeat command
```

