## 🖥️ System Info (Know your machine)
```bash
uname -a     # full system info
hostnamectl  # hostname details
uptime       # how long system is running

free -h      # RAM usage
vmstat       # memory stats
iostat       # disk + CPU stats

lscpu        # CPU info
lsusb        # USB devices
```

---

## 💽 Disk & Filesystem
```bash
df -h                # disk space usage
du -sh dir/          # folder size

lsblk                # disks overview
blkid                # disk info

fdisk -l             # partitions
parted -l            # detailed partitions

mkfs.ext4 /dev/sdX1  # format disk ⚠️
fsck /dev/sdX1       # repair disk

mount /dev/sdX1 /mnt # mount disk
umount /mnt          # unmount

cat /etc/fstab       # auto-mount config
```

---

## 🌐 Networking (Internet & Servers)
```bash
ip addr              # IP address
ip route             # routes

ping -c 4 host       # test connection
traceroute host      # track path

ss -tuln             # open ports
netstat -tuln        # old version

nslookup example.com # DNS lookup
dig example.com      # detailed DNS

curl -I URL          # check website
wget URL             # download file

ssh user@host        # remote login
scp file user@host:/path/  # copy file
sftp user@host       # file transfer

nmap -sS host        # scan ports
ufw enable           # firewall on
ufw allow 22         # allow SSH
```

---

## 📦 Archiving & Compression
```bash
tar -czf file.tar.gz dir/   # compress
tar -xzf file.tar.gz        # extract

zip -r file.zip dir/        # zip folder
unzip file.zip              # unzip

gzip file                   # compress
gunzip file.gz              # decompress

rsync -avz src/ dest/       # sync files
rsync -avz -e ssh src/ user@host:/dest/  # remote sync
```

---

## 📦 Package Management

### Debian / Ubuntu
```bash
apt-get update        # update list
apt-get install pkg   # install
apt-get upgrade       # upgrade
apt-get remove pkg    # remove

apt-cache search pkg  # search
dpkg -i pkg.deb       # install manually
```

### RHEL / Fedora
```bash
yum install pkg
dnf install pkg

rpm -i pkg.rpm
rpm -e pkg
```

